            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="SHE04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Richard Brinsley</forename>
                        <surname>Sheridan</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth notBefore="1751-09" notAfter="1751-10">
                        <placeName>Ireland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1816-07-07"/>
                    <occupation>playwright</occupation>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Richard Brinsley Sheridan was an Irish born dramatist who achieved considerable success on
      the stage with his play <title>The Rivals</title> in 1775. Sheridan subsequetly became close
      to the whigs and was elected to Parliament in 1780. Godwin met Sheridan early in the 1780s and
      wrote for Sheridan's <title>Political Herald</title>.  He had intermittent contact subsequently, seeking 
      Sheridan's advice and support in the writing and prodouction of his tragedies.</p>
                        <p>Godwin records his death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
